<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Taj al-Din Yildiz</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1216">1216</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Tajuddin Yildiz, Taj ad-Din Yildiz, Yildiz of Ghazni</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Taj al-Din Yildiz was a Turkic slave commander of the Ghurid sultan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-of-ghor">Muhammad of Ghor</a> who seized <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghazni">Ghazni</a> after his master's death in 1206. Driven out by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khwarazmians">Khwarazmians</a>, he invaded northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> to claim the Ghurid lands there, but was defeated by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iltutmish">Iltutmish</a> at Tarain in 1216 and put to death.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/taj-al-din-yildiz.jpg" alt="Taj al-Din Yildiz" width="320" height="158" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CNG Coins · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Taj_al-Din_Yildiz._AH_602-612_AD_1206-1215_Ghazna_(Ghazni)_mint._Dated_AH_604_(AD_1207-8).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
